    <h2 class="mb-4">
      Why Financial Institutions in Kenya Need a Loan Management System
    </h2>

    <p>
      Many lending businesses begin with spreadsheets and manual
      records. However, as the number of borrowers and transactions
      increases, these methods can become difficult to maintain.
      Monitoring repayment schedules, updating balances and
      preparing reports may consume valuable staff time.
    </p>

    <p>
      Loan management software helps centralize loan information
      and establish more consistent processes for managing
      repayments, reviewing balances and monitoring overdue
      accounts. It can also make relevant portfolio information
      easier to access when making operational decisions.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4 mb-3">Key Benefits</h3>

    <ul class="list-unstyled vstack gap-2">
      <li>
        <strong>Organized loan records:</strong>
        Keep borrower information and loan details in one system.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Repayment monitoring:</strong>
        Track expected installments against payments received.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Arrears visibility:</strong>
        Identify overdue accounts and prioritize repayment follow-ups.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Improved reporting:</strong>
        Access loan and portfolio information to support management reviews.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reduced repetitive work:</strong>
        Reduce dependence on duplicated spreadsheets and manual recordkeeping.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Centralized access:</strong>
        Work with lending information through a cloud-based platform.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-4">
      By adopting a loan management system in Kenya, lending
      institutions can establish more structured processes for
      managing their portfolios and supporting business growth.
      Actual efficiency gains depend on the organization's
      workflows and how the system is implemented.
    </p>

