    <h2 class="mb-4">Who Uses Loan Management Systems in Kenya?</h2>

    <p>
      Different lending organizations have different requirements.
      The best loan management software should support the way
      your organization issues loans, records repayments and
      monitors its portfolio.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Microfinance Institutions</h3>
    <p>
      Microfinance institutions need organized borrower records,
      repayment tracking, arrears monitoring and portfolio reports.
      A loan management system helps bring these activities
      together and makes relevant loan information easier to review.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">SACCOs</h3>
    <p>
      SACCOs need to manage member loans, repayment schedules
      and interest calculations according to their lending
      arrangements. When evaluating a SACCO loan management
      system, consider member records, reporting requirements
      and the specific lending workflows your SACCO uses.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Digital Lenders</h3>
    <p>
      Digital lending businesses need organized loan records
      and efficient repayment monitoring. When choosing digital
      lending software, assess whether the available features
      support your application, payment, disbursement and
      reporting workflows.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Chamas and Lending Groups</h3>
    <p>
      Chamas and other lending groups can benefit from organized
      borrower records, transparent repayment information and
      clear outstanding balances. A structured loan tracking
      process helps members review lending activity and
      maintain consistent financial records.
    </p>

