<!-- BUYER GUIDE -->

<section class="py-1 bg-white">
  <div class="container article-content">

    <h2 class="mb-4">
      How to Choose the Right Loan Management Software in Kenya
    </h2>

    <p>
      Choosing a loan management system involves more than
      comparing prices. The software should fit your lending
      model, support your reporting needs and make routine
      activities easier to manage.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Loan Calculations and Repayment Schedules</h3>
    <p>
      Check whether the system supports your loan terms,
      interest calculation methods and installment frequencies.
      Test representative loan scenarios to confirm that
      repayment schedules and balances match your requirements.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Arrears and Repayment Monitoring</h3>
    <p>
      Review how the software identifies overdue loans,
      displays outstanding amounts and helps staff prioritize
      repayment follow-ups. Reliable arrears information
      supports more informed portfolio monitoring.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">M-Pesa and Payment Management</h3>
    <p>
      If your borrowers repay through M-Pesa, assess how
      the software handles the payment workflows your
      organization needs. Confirm the supported integration,
      transaction recording and reconciliation processes
      before implementation.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Reports and Financial Information</h3>
    <p>
      Identify the reports required by your management team.
      These may include loan balances, repayment performance,
      arrears and portfolio summaries. Confirm which reports
      are available and whether they meet your needs.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">User Permissions and Data Protection</h3>
    <p>
      Understand how the system manages user roles and
      permissions, protects borrower information and handles
      backups. Access controls should align with your
      organization's internal procedures.
    </p>

    <h3 class="h4 mt-4">Pricing, Implementation and Support</h3>
    <p>
      Compare subscription costs, implementation arrangements,
      training, ongoing support and any additional fees.
      If you are switching from spreadsheets or another
      platform, ask how existing loan records can be migrated.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can also review the
      <a href="/pricing/">
        Repotrans pricing information
      </a>
      when assessing the system against your budget and
      operational requirements.
    </p>

    <p>
      For a more detailed evaluation, read our guide on
      <a href="/blog/how-to-choose-the-right-loan-management-system-in-kenya/">
        how to choose the right loan management system in Kenya
      </a>.
    </p>

  </div>
</section>


